    "body": "fix on issue/4455-holder-form-largest-dia - PR #4469 - pinned by holder_library::shape::tests::a_body_the_flange_envelope_covers_is_not_read_back_smaller, holder_library::shape::tests::each_builtin_taper_holder_reads_back_as_its_shape, egui_app::tests::tool_library_holder_largest::a_copied_holder_shows_the_largest_diameter_of_its_outline_and_applies_as_it_is - merges when reviewed\n\nRoot cause:\n\n1. The form field \"Largest diameter\" held the body steel below the flange (the ER32 nut, Ø50). The drawing states the largest diameter of the whole outline (the BT40 flange, Ø63). The outline was correct. The field is now \"Body diameter\", and a read-only \"Largest diameter\" shows the drawing's value.\n2. A second defect is under the safety floor. `HolderShape::of` read a shrink-fit body that the flange envelope covers back as the narrowest body that draws the outline. A longer gauge length then drew the body smaller than the steel. `of` now refuses such an outline, except for a library chuck at its library gauge length. The form refuses to write a shape that does not read back as itself.\n\nPR #4438 (`edit_user_holder`) is affected. The details are in a comment on #4438.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
