    "updated_at": "2026-11-27T23:12:51Z",
    "body": "Priority raised from P3 to P1.\n\nThe work on PR #4469 found a safety-floor defect behind the label mismatch. On a shrink-fit holder whose flange envelope covers the body, `HolderShape::of` reads back a body that is smaller than the real steel (for example 41.544 mm for the 42 mm body of \"BT40 Shrink 20 mm\"). A write of those values can draw a holder outline that is smaller than the steel. Holder outlines go into the collision checks, so a check can pass when the real holder collides.\n\nPR #4438 (`edit_user_holder`) merged to `main` at 22:54Z. It writes through `HolderShape::geometry`, so `main` now has this write path through MCP. PR #4469 gets these changes before review:\n- a merge of `main`;\n- the MCP write changed to `HolderShape::component`, which refuses a shape that does not read back as itself;\n- the MCP test fixture moved to a gauge length where the body shows;\n- the library shrink exception limited, or its residual risk documented.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
